# Resource Envelope -- ignore rules for C++/CMake build residue only.
#
# Rule of thumb: this file ignores outputs, never inputs. Sources, headers, tests, test data,
# documentation, packaging metadata, CMakeLists.txt, and the *.cmake modules under cmake/ are
# intentional deliverables and must stay tracked.

# --- Build trees -----------------------------------------------------------
build/
out/
cmake-build-*/
.vs/
# .vscode/ is deliberately not ignored wholesale: shared settings.json and launch.json are useful
# and reviewable. Only editor-local residue (below) is ignored.

# --- CMake residue (also catches an accidental in-source configure) --------
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
Testing/
install_manifest.txt
compile_commands.json
# Generated configure output (*.cmake.in -> *.cmake) is always written inside the build tree, which
# the build-tree rules above already cover. The templates under cmake/ are source: never ignore
# *.cmake or *.cmake.in globally.

# --- Compiled artifacts ----------------------------------------------------
*.obj
*.o
*.a
*.lib
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.idb
*.gcda
*.gcno
*.dSYM/

# --- Visual Studio user state ---------------------------------------------
*.user
*.suo
*.sln.docstates

# --- OS junk ---------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
desktop.ini
